{"id": "740094062371274783", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:29:34.752000+00:00", "content": "[attachment: unknown.png]", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740094089604759573", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:29:41.245000+00:00", "content": "epic", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740094200258887740", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:30:07.627000+00:00", "content": "``SMS_MakeMActorsWithAnmData`` allocates an array which stores each mactor\nand returns the array", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740094314540957736", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:30:34.874000+00:00", "content": "but this function passes 1 as the count and just returns the first item in the array", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740094367943098409", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:30:47.606000+00:00", "content": "leaking the array", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740094932416462918", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "shibboleet", "author_id": "519168521918349312", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T06:33:02.187000+00:00", "content": "wow", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740119273728376952", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Noki Doki", "author_id": "170141360375070720", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:09:45.608000+00:00", "content": "There's another memory leak where each tree leaf allocates its own collision object, but then the tree allocates another collision object and sets it over the original", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740119581850468396", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Noki Doki", "author_id": "170141360375070720", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:10:59.070000+00:00", "content": "Ultimately it doesn't matter that much since the game uses `freeAll` on the main heap before loading the next level, but yeah", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740121496210505759", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:18:35.489000+00:00", "content": "i find memory management interesting\nthe game uses a stack-based heap for gameplay", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740121661520478238", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:19:14.902000+00:00", "content": "all objects in the scene are in the game heap\nyou can free only the tail, everything, or nothing", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740121820979658783", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:19:52.920000+00:00", "content": "for instance if you were to use a single ``std::string`` -- boom, memory leak", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740121989645074482", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:20:33.133000+00:00", "content": "it'll try but it can't free that shit in its destructor, it'll just silently fail and output it through the console", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740122061367672842", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:20:50.233000+00:00", "content": "```cpp\nvoid JKRSolidHeap::free(void * ptr) {\n    JUTWarningConsole_f(\"free: cannot free memory block (%08x)\\n\", ptr);\n}\n```", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740122338573549631", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Made 🐬", "author_id": "148544281106186240", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:21:56.324000+00:00", "content": "Is it really a leak when it's freed when the stack gets popped?", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740122575988064267", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Noki Doki", "author_id": "170141360375070720", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:22:52.928000+00:00", "content": "Yeah you can't even free the tail because the heap doesn't see individual objects, only how much is allocated overall", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740122930796560426", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Noki Doki", "author_id": "170141360375070720", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:24:17.521000+00:00", "content": "All it can do is free everything at once, so memory leaks are contained", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740123405679853579", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:26:10.742000+00:00", "content": "technically the game itself has memory leaks if you, say, add an object to a ``TViewObjPtrListT``", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740123525372837908", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:26:39.279000+00:00", "content": "since it uses ``std::vector`` it'll try to resize the array and fail to free the old one", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740123632289710090", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Made 🐬", "author_id": "148544281106186240", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:27:04.770000+00:00", "content": "Oh, do they use Realloc anywhere ?", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740123648672661564", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:27:08.676000+00:00", "content": "but SMS needn't worry about that because ``JDrama`` uses reserve before adding objects", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
{"id": "740123710060625972", "channel_id": "736052549001674884", "author": "Deleted User", "author_id": "456226577798135808", "timestamp": "2020-08-04T08:27:23.312000+00:00", "content": "but after that it's fair game", "reply_to": null, "attachments": [], "reactions": []}
